Falsifies `system_tests::user::package_index_tests::a_package_is_fetched_through_the_index_by_name_over_tls_and_judged_by_its_digest`,
row 35 of notes/confinement-claims.md (a listed location never reaches a private or link-local
address).

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is the rebinding escape milestone 871 (a sixth outsider pass attacks the confinement
claim) booted: the package client checks one resolution of a listed location's host, then
connects by name, which resolves again. `helpers/name-server-peer` answers `rebind.basalt.test`
public on a boot's first query and at the private peer after, so the connect reaches 10.0.2.9.

Expected to fail: `the_rebinding_probe_reached_no_private_peer`'s assertion that the listed
location's reason carries no `Tls(`, with the private peer's
`Tls(InvalidCertificate(NotValidForNameContext { expected: DnsName("rebind.basalt.test"), ...`.
Confirmed red on 2026-10-19 (UTC) at `system_tests/src/user/package_index_tests.rs:206` on
aarch64, riscv64 and x86_64, with `script/test --arch <a> --test a_package_is_fetched_through`,
and green on aarch64 with the patch reverted. The hunk is portable code, so one patch serves every
leg.

